{"id": 3, "ts": 1780637714.984865, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019d like to start the discussion by putting forward Candidate\u202fB as the leading option.\u202fFrom my notes, Candidate\u202fB is very conscientious, which speaks directly to operational reliability, and handles stress very well\u2014critical for long\u2011distance flights where unexpected events are common.\u202fTheir excellent computer skills and strong ability to assess weather conditions also demonstrate solid technical competence and sound decision\u2011making under pressure.\u202fThe main concerns are interpersonal: they are regarded as pretentious and sometimes adopt the wrong tone when communicating. While these issues could affect crew cooperation and professional communication, they appear less severe than the more fundamental gaps seen in the other candidates (e.g., Candidate\u202fC\u2019s egocentric attitude and lack of willingness to develop, Candidate\u202fD\u2019s moodiness and loner reputation, Candidate\u202fA\u2019s unfriendly demeanor and health concerns).\u202fThus, I believe Candidate\u202fB offers the strongest overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role, provided we can address the communication style during onboarding."}
